        content: `**This week — 20 minutes:**

**Step 1 — Test HoH if you're unmarried.** Did you pay >50% of housing costs? Did anyone qualifying live with you >50% of the year? If yes to both, you've been overpaying on Single.

**Step 2 — If married, run both MFJ and MFS.** Most tax software lets you toggle. Only choose MFS if it saves money OR you're protecting yourself from a spouse's tax issues. Remember MFS kills the **student loan interest deduction**, **education credits**, and **Saver's Credit**.

**Step 3 — Audit your dependents.** Check elderly parents — if their **gross income is under $5,200** (Social Security doesn't count) and you cover >50% of their support, claim them for the **$500 Credit for Other Dependents**. Check adult children up to age 24 if full-time students.

**Step 4 — Amend prior returns.** You have **3 years** to file Form 1040-X. A missed HoH status on three returns can be **$5,000+** back to you.`,
