        type: "example",
        title: "A Year in the Life: The Chen Family",
        content: `**Robert & Mei Chen**, dual-income MFJ, **$220k AGI**, two kids, $400k brokerage, $1.1M combined 401(k)s, $90k Roths. Here's one year on the calendar:\n\n**Jan:** Mei updates W-4 after her raise (new income $30k higher) — avoids April surprise.\n**Feb:** They file early; **$3,200 refund** (close to their ±$500 target — could be tighter).\n**Mar:** Decide to keep using their CPA — Mei has RSUs and ISOs.\n**Apr 15:** Each maxes **$7,000 Roth IRA** (prior year).\n**Jun:** Mid-year — YTD gains **$8,400**. Set up DAF.\n**Sep:** Robert sells **$30k RSUs** at vest — coordinates with CPA.\n**Nov:** CPA call — projects **$4,800 owed**. Plan: harvest **$3,000 losses**, **donate $25k of appreciated stock** to DAF.\n**Dec 20:** Execute — TLH done, DAF funded, **FSA $400 left** → buy glasses.\n**Result:** Tax bill drops from **$4,800 owed to $300 refund**. Net annual savings: **~$8,500**.`,
