        type: "example",
        title: "Maya, Age 35, Building All Three Buckets",
        content: `**Maya** earns **$95k** as a project manager. Here's her annual retirement split:\n\n- **Tax-Deferred**: $12,000 to Traditional 401(k) — drops her taxable income to $83k, saving **~$2,640** at the 22% bracket.\n- **Tax-Free**: $7,000 to Roth IRA + $4,300 to **HSA** (employee + employer combined) = **$11,300** going into tax-free buckets. HSA gets a triple tax break: deductible in, grows tax-free, withdraws tax-free for medical.\n- **Taxable**: $300/month ($3,600/year) into a brokerage VTI position. After 30 years at 7%, this grows to **~$340k** with a cost basis of $108k — gains taxed at LTCG rates only when sold.\n\nAt age 65, Maya has roughly **$1.1M Traditional**, **$900k Roth+HSA**, **$340k taxable**. She can now engineer withdrawals — pulling from whichever bucket keeps her in the lowest combined tax bracket each year. **This is true financial flexibility.**`,
