        type: "application",
        title: "Open Your Self-Employed Plan",
        content: `**Step 1 — Confirm you qualify.** You need self-employment income reported on Schedule C, K-1 (active partner), or a 1099-NEC. W-2 income alone doesn't unlock these accounts. **Step 2 — Calculate your contribution limit.** Use net SE earnings × 92.35% (the half-SE-tax adjustment), then apply the 25% / $23,500 formulas. Schwab, Fidelity, and Vanguard all publish free calculators. **Step 3 — Open the account by December 31.** Solo 401(k) **must be established by Dec 31** of the contribution year (funded by your tax deadline). SEP IRAs can be opened AND funded right up to your extended deadline (Oct 15) — handy if you forgot. **Step 4 — Roll old 401(k)s into the new Solo 401(k).** Consolidates accounts and revives backdoor Roth eligibility. **Step 5 — File Form 5500-EZ** once your Solo 401(k) balance crosses **$250,000** at year-end.`,
