        type: "example",
        title: "$500K Portfolio, 30 Years",
        content: `**Maria, age 35**, has a **$500K portfolio**: 70% stocks / 30% bonds. She splits it across $200K Roth IRA, $200K Traditional 401(k), and $100K taxable. **30-year horizon, 24% federal tax bracket.**

**The naive setup (random placement):** She holds the same 70/30 mix in EVERY account. Bonds throw off taxable interest in the taxable account. Growth stocks accumulate gains in the Traditional IRA (eventually taxed as ordinary income on withdrawal).

After 30 years: **~$3.05 million** after taxes.

**The optimized setup (location-aware):**
- **Roth IRA ($200K):** 100% small-cap + emerging markets index — tax-free growth on the highest-return assets
- **Traditional 401(k) ($200K):** All bonds + REITs — ordinary income trapped inside the wrapper
- **Taxable ($100K):** Total US market index + international (foreign tax credit) — LTCG-favored

Same 70/30 overall allocation. After 30 years: **~$3.16 million** after taxes.

**Difference: $110,000 — for an afternoon of rearranging trades.** No extra risk, no extra contribution, no extra anything. That's a free retirement vacation home every decade.`,
