        content: `**By account type**:

**401(k)/403(b)**: You're stuck with the menu. Pick the **cheapest index fund** offered — usually a mutual fund. Look for any fund with **'500 Index'** or **'Total Stock Market Index'** in the name, ER under **0.20%**.

**Roth IRA / Traditional IRA**: Either works. If you want **automatic $583/month** investing, mutual funds (VTSAX, FZROX) win on simplicity. If you prefer tickers and intraday flexibility, ETFs (VTI, ITOT) win.

**Taxable brokerage**: **ETFs**. Period. VTI for US, VXUS for international, BND for bonds.

**HSA**: Most HSA custodians (Fidelity HSA especially) let you buy ETFs commission-free. **VTI or FZROX**.

**Action this week**: 1) List every brokerage account you have. 2) Look at what's inside each. 3) If you have a **mutual fund in a taxable brokerage**, plan to swap to the equivalent ETF (consider tax cost of selling first — may be better to just direct **new contributions** to the ETF).`,
