        type: "intro",
        title: "Your Brain Is Not Built for Investing",
        content: `In **2002**, psychologist **Daniel Kahneman** won the **Nobel Prize in Economics** — not for an economic model, but for proving humans are **systematically irrational** about money. His research with **Amos Tversky** (called **Prospect Theory**) showed a brutal truth: a **$100 loss feels about 2x worse** than a **$100 gain feels good**.

That single asymmetry — **loss aversion** — explains why your neighbor sold all his stocks in **March 2020** at the **COVID bottom** and missed the **+75% rally** that followed. Why your uncle dumped his **Vanguard funds** in **2008** at the bottom. Why someone always 'just waiting for a better entry point' never actually buys.

This lesson covers the **four big cognitive biases** that destroy returns — and the **simple systems** that disarm them. The good news: you don't need willpower. You need **automation**.`,
