        explanation: "**Do nothing.** This is the answer for nearly every market crash question. **Loss aversion** is screaming at you to sell, but Vanguard's data shows that investors who **stay the course** and keep contributing during downturns dramatically outperform those who flee to cash. Your automatic contributions are now buying shares **22% cheaper** — this is exactly when dollar-cost averaging pays off. Market timing requires being right **twice** (when to sell AND when to buy back), and almost nobody succeeds at both. The Vanguard 'Time in market' study found that missing just the 10 best days over 20 years cuts returns nearly in half.",
