        content: `Walk into **bogleheads.org** — the forum named after Vanguard founder **John Bogle** — and you'll find tens of thousands of regular people who became millionaires using a **strict 9-step sequence**. No stock picking. No market timing. No advisor. Just **discipline applied to a checklist**.

The Boglehead philosophy comes from Bogle's book **'The Little Book of Common Sense Investing'** (2007) and the community's own **'Bogleheads' Guide to Investing'**. Their motto: **'Simplicity is the master key to financial success.'**

This lesson lays out the **exact step-by-step priority order** — what to fund first with each new dollar, then the next, then the next. Most people skip steps (maxing 401(k) before taking the employer match, paying down a 3% mortgage before maxing Roth IRA). The order matters because **dollars at the top of the list earn far more than dollars at the bottom**. Master the sequence and you've solved 95% of personal investing.`,
