        content: `**Build your plan today** (one sheet of paper):

**Section 1 — My step right now**: Look at the 9 steps. What's the **lowest-numbered** step where I have **unfilled capacity**? That's where my next $100 goes.

**Section 2 — My target allocation**: Pick one based on age and risk tolerance. Example **age-based**: bonds % = age - 20. Age 35 → 15% bonds, 85% stocks. Of stocks: 70% US + 30% international.

**Section 3 — My three tickers**:
- US: **VTI** (or **VTSAX** mutual)
- International: **VXUS** (or **VTIAX**)
- Bonds: **BND** (or **VBTLX**)

**Section 4 — My rebalance day**: Pick a date — **January 15** — when I check allocation and rebalance back to target if drift exceeds **5%**.

**Section 5 — My rules**: 'I will not sell during downturns. I will not chase trends. I will increase contributions when I get raises. I will check this plan once per quarter.' **Sign it. Date it.**

That's the **entire plan**. Stay the course. Become a millionaire on autopilot.`,
